=== 3. THE FIX DID NOT OVERSHOOT -- transfers are still LISTED -- PASS ===
This was the first thing I checked, because dropping transfers from the results
would trade the attempt-1 bug for a worse one.

Driver (scratchpad copy) over a five-row fixture chosen so no sign accident can
hide an error: Income +5000, Outflow -1200, Outflow +50 (a refund), Transfer
-3000 (outbound), Transfer +700 (INBOUND -- so the transfer subtotal is not
uniformly negative). Raw tool output:

  search_transactions {}  ->
   {"page":1,"per_page":50,"sum_amount":3850,"total":5,"total_pages":1,
    "transactions":[
      {"amount":700,"date":"2026-08-11","description":"USAA FUNDS TRANSFER IN","type":"Transfer"},
      {"amount":-3000,"date":"2026-08-09","description":"SCHWAB FUNDS TRANSFER","type":"Transfer"},
      {"amount":50,"date":"2026-08-08","description":"GROCERY STORE REFUND","type":"Outflow"},
      {"amount":-1200,"date":"2026-08-07","description":"GROCERY STORE","type":"Outflow"},
      {"amount":5000,"date":"2026-08-05","description":"PAYROLL DIRECT DEP","type":"Income"}]}

Both halves hold: total=5 counts the transfers, BOTH Transfer rows appear in the
page, and sum_amount=3850 = 5000 + (-1200) + 50, the Income+Outflow sum. The
user can still see money they actually moved.

Pagination carries them too, so they are not being dropped one layer down:
  {"per_page":2}          -> total=5, total_pages=3, page 1 = the two Transfer rows
  {"per_page":2,"page":3} -> total=5, total_pages=3, page 3 = the Income row
A fix that had dropped transfers would report total=3 / total_pages=2 here.

Default path narrowed to a transfer-only window:
  {"start_date":"2026-08-09","end_date":"2026-08-11"} ->
    total=2, both Transfer rows returned, sum_amount=0
Correct and documented (rows listed, sum over Income+Outflow of an empty set).

The sum is computed AFTER the amount filter, not over the unfiltered set:
  {"min_amount":1000} -> total=3 (transfer -3000, outflow -1200, income 5000),
                         sum_amount=3800 = 5000 + (-1200). Correct.

