 n) The old false clauses are gone -- grep over server.go for "CANNOT be
    answered", "filtered out at LOAD", "no \"transfer\" transaction type",
    "do NOT show savings" returns nothing.

I checked specifically for the A1-attempt-3 shape (a description asserting the
inverse of the code in a machine-facing contract no test reads) and did not find
it. The one place the two documents are in tension rather than contradiction:
(j) says the spending tools do not count transfers "in their totals", while
search_transactions with type="transfer" returns sum_amount -2300, which is a
total of transfers. That is the caller explicitly asking for them, and the tool's
own description -- the more specific contract, (e) -- states that rule
