=== Ruling 2026-08-16e (loop assertions) -- two advisory notes, not defects ===
 - The two new tests have no loops. TestSearchTransactionsFiltersByTypeTransfer
   indexes out.Transactions[0] after `if out.Total != 1 { t.Fatalf }`; Total is
   the match count rather than len(out.Transactions), so on a hypothetical
   paging regression this panics rather than reporting cleanly. It cannot pass
   vacuously, which is what the ruling protects against.
 - anchor_test.go's three "nothing was written" loops (:46, :129, :298) still
   range over `accts` with no preceding assertion that accts is non-empty --
   the same note I raised at attempt 1, unchanged because attempt 2 did not
   touch that file. My item-9 fingerprint driver covers that ground with a
   sensitivity control, so the BEHAVIOR is verified; this remains a
   test-robustness note.
 - Also noted: server_test.go's TestServerInstructionsCarryLoadBearingClaims
   pins ~40 claims but attempt 2 added only "Four tools are guarded" to it. The
   new transfer sentences -- "do NOT COUNT", "Five LEDGER tools", the
   get_transfers sign convention -- are load-bearing by that test's own stated
   purpose and are not pinned, so a future behavior change could falsify them
   silently. Advisory: the claims are true today, verified above by driving, and
   the brief's item 7 asks that they be true and use GLOSSARY vocabulary, which
   they are and do (Transfer, TransferClass, Internal transfer, BalanceAnchor,
   with GLOSSARY.md cited by name).

